# GitHub Issues for Research

The researcher monitors GitHub issues with the `research-request` label.

## Create a Research Request

```bash
# Create a single issue
gh issue create --repo gitopedia/gitopedia \
  --title "Topic Name" \
  --body "Research request for an encyclopedia article." \
  --label "research-request"

# Examples
gh issue create --repo gitopedia/gitopedia --title "Quantum Computing" --label "research-request" --body "Research request"
gh issue create --repo gitopedia/gitopedia --title "French Revolution" --label "research-request" --body "Research request"
```

## List Open Requests

```bash
gh issue list --repo gitopedia/gitopedia --label "research-request" --state open
```

## Bulk Create Issues

```bash
# Create multiple topics
$topics = @("Artificial Intelligence", "Black Holes", "Renaissance Art")
foreach ($topic in $topics) {
    gh issue create --repo gitopedia/gitopedia --title $topic --label "research-request" --body "Research request"
}
```

## Issue Lifecycle

1. **Created** with `research-request` label
2. **Processing** - Researcher picks it up
3. **PR Created** - Article draft in PR
4. **Merged** - Article published
5. **Closed** - Issue auto-closed when PR merges

## Labels Used

| Label | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `research-request` | Request for new article |
| `research:status-discovery` | Discovery step complete |
| `research:status-summarized` | Summarization complete |
| `research:status-drafted` | Draft ready |
| `research:manual-review` | Waiting for human review |
